nal Republican environment could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Steven Horsford (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Steven Horsford seeks another term in a Las Vegas-area district that leans Democratic by about two points. He enters the general election with a large financial edge, having raised over $4 million to Cody Whipple's $1.2 million, and retains most of it for the campaign's final stretch. Whipple, a small-town rancher running on border security and election integrity, has drawn some local attention but little outside spending.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and expert assessments. Ratings cluster at Likely D, with several outlets calling it Safe or Solid D, and prediction markets price Democratic chances around 95%. The race has flown under the radar compared with Nevada's other House contests, consistent with an incumbent comfortably favored but not invulnerable.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9628, "margin": 12.37}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9577, "margin": 12.4}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9615, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9427, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9481, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9627, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9594, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9636, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9624, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 12.3}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9555, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9434, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9455, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.941, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "20